#
# ✒ Description:
#     Line-ending and packaging policy for the toolMan ecosystem. Every text
#     file is stored and checked out as LF on all platforms, keeping the UTF-8
#     headers (and the house signature glyphs) byte-stable across Windows,
#     macOS, and Linux checkouts.
#
# ✒ Key Features:
#     - text=auto eol=lf: one line ending everywhere, enforced by
#       scripts/check.mjs (hygiene)
#     - Binary declarations so images, fonts, and archives never get
#       line-ending conversion or textual diffs
#     - export-ignore on development-only paths: a downloaded ZIP or the CI
#       "toolman-site" package is just the app, ready to open or host
#
# ✒ Other Important Information:
#     - Dependencies: git
#     - Compatible platforms: any git client; GitHub honours export-ignore
#       for Download ZIP and release source archives
#     - Clones are unaffected: export-ignore only shapes archives, so a
#       contributor's checkout still has the tests and scripts
# ==============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Development-only paths stay out of archives (git archive / Download ZIP)
.github/ export-ignore
.vscode/ export-ignore
scripts/ export-ignore
tests/ export-ignore
tools/*/tests/ export-ignore
.editorconfig export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
.gitignore export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
